---
import RedlineLayout from '../layouts/RedlineLayout.astro';
import RedlineCTA from '../components/redline/RedlineCTA.astro';
---

<RedlineLayout
  title="Herru Adi · Strategic Design Partner"
  description="I help startups and growing teams figure out what to build, how to build it, and why it matters. Then I make it real."
  active=""
>
  <style>
    .hero {
      padding: 64px 0 56px;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule-strong);
    }
    .hero-grid {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 48px;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .hero-grid > .hero-main {
      flex: 1 1 480px;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .hero-grid {
        flex-direction: column;
      }
    }
    .brief-label {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      color: var(--ink3);
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .brief {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.9;
      max-width: 60ch;
      color: var(--ink3);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }
    .margin-note {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--acc-ink);
      margin-top: 18px;
    }
    .verdict {
      font-family: var(--sans);
      font-stretch: 62%;
      font-weight: 850;
      font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 8.6vw, 7.4rem);
      line-height: 0.88;
      letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-top: 36px;
      max-width: 12ch;
    }
    .hero-side {
      flex: 0 1 260px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--rule-strong);
    }
    .hero-side .block {
      padding: 14px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .hero-side .block:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .hero-side .block p:not(.tb-label) {
      font-size: 14.5px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: var(--ink2);
    }
    .hero-side .block .tb-label {
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .yrs-num {
      font-family: var(--sans);
      font-stretch: 62%;
      font-weight: 850;
      font-size: 44px;
      line-height: 0.9;
    }
    .yrs-label {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      color: var(--ink2);
    }
    .manifesto {
      padding: 88px 0 96px;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-main">
        <p class="brief-label">Client Brief, As Received</p>
        <div class="brief">
          <p data-rr-type style="--t:0ms;--d:450ms"><span class="rr-strike" data-rr-bar style="--t:520ms">"We need a landing page that looks premium and converts."</span></p>
          <p data-rr-type style="--t:150ms;--d:560ms">
            <span class="rr-strike" data-rr-bar style="--t:720ms">"Something like Stripe, or Linear. Modern. Clean."</span>
            <span class="rr-strike" data-rr-bar style="--t:920ms">"Maybe a gradient hero."</span>
          </p>
          <p data-rr-type style="--t:300ms;--d:400ms"><span class="rr-strike" data-rr-bar style="--t:1060ms">"Can you also make the logo bigger?"</span></p>
        </div>

        <p class="margin-note" data-rr-note style="--t:1320ms">
          → none of this is the brief. it's a mood board.<br />
          → what are you actually asking people to believe?
        </p>

        <h1 class="verdict">
          <span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:0">Great</span>
          <span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:1">design</span>
          <span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:2">won't</span>
          <span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:3">save</span>
          <span class="rr-hl" data-rr-hl><span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:4">a</span> <span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:5">broken</span> <span class="rr-w" data-rr-w style="--i:6">business.</span></span>
        </h1>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-side">
        <div class="block">
          <p class="tb-label">Standing Question</p>
          <p>"Is this actually the problem?" Asked before Figma opens, on every engagement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="block">
          <p class="tb-label">Method</p>
          <p>Two modes: interrogate the brief, or execute it with precision once it holds up. One standard either way, make it count.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="block">
          <span class="yrs-num">9</span>
          <span class="yrs-label">YRS PRACTICE</span>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CASE LOG ============ -->
  <section id="work">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="tag mono upper">Case Log</p>
        <h2>Three problems, diagnosed and rebuilt.</h2>
      </div>
      <a href="/work">Full case log →</a>
    </div>

    <article class="case">
      <div class="case-rev mono">REV<b>01</b></div>
      <div>
        <p class="case-meta">F&amp;B SaaS · UI/UX Lead · 0-to-1</p>
        <h3 class="case-title">AYCE</h3>
        <dl class="fields">
          <div class="field"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>Kitchen operations running on memory and panic.</dd></div>
          <div class="field"><dt>Build</dt><dd>A system so simple, it runs itself.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="tags"><span>SaaS</span><span>Operations Design</span><span>0-to-1</span></p>
        <a class="case-link" href="/work/ayce">Read the case study →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-status"><span class="status-pill">Shipped</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="case">
      <div class="case-rev mono">REV<b>02</b></div>
      <div>
        <p class="case-meta">Property Management System · Product Design Lead · Middle East</p>
        <h3 class="case-title">Hoteely</h3>
        <dl class="fields">
          <div class="field"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>Hotel management scattered across too many screens.</dd></div>
          <div class="field"><dt>Build</dt><dd>One clean, intuitive screen that replaced the chaos.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="tags"><span>Enterprise</span><span>Dashboard Design</span></p>
        <a class="case-link" href="/work/hoteely">Read the case study →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-status"><span class="status-pill">Shipped</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="case">
      <div class="case-rev mono">REV<b>03</b></div>
      <div>
        <p class="case-meta">AI Crypto Dashboard · Solo Designer · UK Client</p>
        <h3 class="case-title">Vantagelab</h3>
        <dl class="fields">
          <div class="field"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>Market noise, and a first-time crypto founder losing to complexity.</dd></div>
          <div class="field"><dt>Build</dt><dd>Clarity, without dumbing the data down.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="tags"><span>AI</span><span>Data Visualization</span></p>
        <a class="case-link" href="/work/vantagelab">Read the case study →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-status"><span class="status-pill">Shipped</span></div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ MANIFESTO STAMP ============ -->
  <section class="manifesto">
    <div class="stamp stamp-plain">
      <p class="sund">&ldquo;Hidup harus berguna bagi sesama.&rdquo;</p>
      <p class="eng">Life should be useful to others.</p>
      <p class="seal">Not a tagline, the operating principle. Also my son's name: Gunaka Sasama.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FIELD NOTES ============ -->
  <section id="blog">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="tag mono upper">Field Notes</p>
        <h2>Thinking out loud, in writing.</h2>
      </div>
      <a href="/blog">All notes →</a>
    </div>

    <a class="note" href="/blog/the-most-expensive-design-mistake">
      <span class="note-cat">Business × Design</span>
      <span class="note-title">The most expensive design mistake isn't bad UI, it's building the wrong thing</span>
      <span class="note-arrow">read →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="note" href="/blog/designing-for-crypto">
      <span class="note-cat">Field Notes</span>
      <span class="note-title">Designing for crypto when you know nothing about crypto</span>
      <span class="note-arrow">read →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="note" href="/blog/kitchen-chaos-saas">
      <span class="note-cat">Field Notes</span>
      <span class="note-title">What kitchen chaos taught me about SaaS product design</span>
      <span class="note-arrow">read →</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <RedlineCTA />
</RedlineLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var root = document.documentElement;
    if (root.dataset.rr !== 'play') return;
    function settle() { root.dataset.rr = 'done'; off(); }
    function off() { ['scroll', 'wheel', 'touchmove', 'keydown'].forEach(function (e) { removeEventListener(e, settle); }); }
    ['scroll', 'wheel', 'touchmove', 'keydown'].forEach(function (e) { addEventListener(e, settle, { passive: true }); });
    setTimeout(settle, 3200);
  })();
</script>
